  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">I am Lin Zhu, a staff engineer in Montreal. For about twelve years I have built the systems other engineers rely on: automation frameworks first, then internal tooling and shared services, and for the last stretch AI agents running in production.</p>
  <p>I came in through a mathematics degree and a master's in computer science, and I still think of most of this work as the same problem: find the friction between people and their systems, then build the thing that removes it.</p>
  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>A personal notebook, written in the open. Right now most posts are about AI agents, because that is what I have been building. Over time the mix will drift toward whatever I am working on: tooling, automation, engineering habits, the occasional note on how a career in this field actually goes. The <a href="/">topic chips</a> on the writing page are the map.</p>
  <p>Every post is one idea, short, with a diagram or a comparison where words would take longer. Everything here is my own view, written in general terms. No employer specifics.</p>
  <h2>Two languages</h2>
  <p>Posts appear in English first. Some also have a Chinese version, written for Chinese readers rather than translated; the language switch in the header takes you to it when one exists.</p>
